<p>MIME is the format an email or a multipart HTTP request travels in: headers, a body, and possibly nested
parts with their own headers. <code>pop-mime</code> reads that format into objects and writes it back out.
<code>pop-mail</code> and <code>pop-http</code> both build on it, so most applications meet it indirectly — you reach for it
directly when you have a raw message in hand, or need a part shaped in a way the higher-level component
does not offer.</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
